    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for high offensive output today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Kyle Tucker** (78.08), our two strongest plays. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits immensely from a favorable encounter with Griffin Canning, as high park factors and positive SP skill projections combine with a top-of-the-order boost to solidify his elite status. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** faces Anthony Kay; while the matchup against a southpaw is traditionally neutral, the wind-out conditions and favorable SP skill metrics make him a must-start despite the projected sixth-spot placement. **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) also enters elite territory, boosted by his high-frequency stolen base environment against Shane Baz, where the slow delivery of the opposing starter provides a meaningful edge for our speed-oriented strategy.\n\nThe most difficult decision for today's lineup involved the benching of **Josh Jung** (52.36), who narrowly missed the cut behind the surging **Curtis Mead** (51.27) and **Coby Mayo** (53.35). While **Josh Jung** possesses strong park factors, the optimizer favored the dynamic platoon edges for **Curtis Mead** against Bryce Miller and the raw power potential of **Coby Mayo** against Griffin Canning. We are keeping a close watch on **Liam Hicks**, whose score of 45.23 sits right at the edge of our efficiency floor. Although he is projected in the leadoff spot, the matchup against Braxton Ashcraft presents the highest risk of the day due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill profile. All managers should note that these scores assume standard batting order projections; any late-breaking lineup changes shifting **Liam Hicks**, **Miguel Vargas**, or **Sam Antonacci** down the order would necessitate an immediate re-evaluation of their viability to preserve our limited game caps.",
